  "slides": [
    {
      "id": "R01Grd",
      "number": 1,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/001.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "AWS + Datadog Securing the blind spot in your pipeline Daniel « phrawzty » Maher Senior Security Advocate & Researcher",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "3Jk4k2",
      "number": 2,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/002.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "ç Do you really know what’s in your stack? 2",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "fdSscR",
      "number": 3,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/003.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "What the data tell us npm PyPI RubyGems crates.io Hex.pm Packagist Max Auth (Human) 3 3 0 1 0 0 4 Auth (Machine) 6 4 4 4 2 2 7 Access Control 6 4 4 4 5 4 7 Build & Provenance 6 4 3 2 2 2 8 Integrity & Signing 5 5 6 2 3 2 6 Vulnerability Mgmt 7 3 4 3 4 4 7 Abuse Prevention 6 5 5 5 5 2 6 Transparency 5 4 5 3 3 2 7 3",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "HxBgUq",
      "number": 4,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/004.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "The gaps that matter ● Authentication ○ optional controls are not actually controls ● Provenance ○ no guarantee that the package actually comes from the source ● Build ○ none of the registries enforce isolated build environments 4",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "uGuUNF",
      "number": 5,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/005.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "The gaps that matter ● Authentication ○ optional controls are not actually controls ● Provenance ○ no guarantee that the package actually comes from the source ● Build ○ none of the registries enforce isolated build environments Registries are not your security team. They are infrastructure. 5",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "WadIFe",
      "number": 6,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/006.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "AI amplifies the problem ● AI Assistants add dependencies automatically ● The last point of human friction has now disappeared ● What was already largely invisible is now even faster 6",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "8uM683",
      "number": 7,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/007.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "2 in the morning… a maintainer is compromised a malicious package is published an automated « latest » build runs 7",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "lE4u0S",
      "number": 8,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/008.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "AWS CodeArtifact: the preventive control ● Managed artefact repository service ● Compatible with npm, pip, Maven, NuGet, etc… ● Your tools, your workflow ● You decide what gets in 8",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "NXnhsr",
      "number": 9,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/009.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Control architecture 9",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "zrWVlG",
      "number": 10,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/010.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Three barriers ● Architectural isolation ○ your builds never talk to public registries ● Automated validation ○ every new version is scanned before a decision is made ● Explicit promotion ○ by default, nothing gets through (spoiler : version pinning) 10",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "cBFJdf",
      "number": 11,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/011.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Three barriers ● Architectural isolation ○ your builds never talk to public registries ● Automated validation ○ every new version is scanned before a decision is made ● Explicit promotion ○ by default, nothing gets through (spoiler : version pinning) 11",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "EUy7W4",
      "number": 12,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/012.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Datadog Code Security SCA SAST Software Composition Analysis Static Code Analysis Secret Scanning IAST (just that) Runtime Code Analysis 12",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "qogvOT",
      "number": 13,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/013.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Datadog Code Security SCA SAST Software Composition Analysis Static Code Analysis Secret Scanning IAST (que ça) Runtime Code Analysis 13",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "T8PjGs",
      "number": 14,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/014.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "6 months later… malicious package published (oops) vulnerability in prod (OOPS) time to panic ?! 14",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "5S8X9H",
      "number": 15,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/015.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Six months later ● SCA « active » (Software Composition Analysis) ○ the vulnerable package is detected (service, version, CVE, etc.) ● IAST (Interactive Application Security Testing) ○ the exec path is detected and the impact is confirmed 15",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "hlrL1g",
      "number": 16,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/016.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Preventive vs. Detective ● Preventive : block before it gets in ○ CodeArtifact, SAST, SCA (static mode) ● Detective : know what’s already there — and act ○ SCA (active mode), IAST 16",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "K5a8u5",
      "number": 17,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/017.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "ç AWS et Datadog together = defence in depth 17",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "wPIwmU",
      "number": 18,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/018.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Where to start? ● Map your dependency graph — know what you’re building on ● Identify your source registries ● Establish a preventive control layer ● Ensure full production visibility 18",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "Yj1ket",
      "number": 19,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/019.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Where to start? ● Map your dependency graph — know what you’re building on ● Identify your source registries ● Establish a preventive control layer ● Ensure full production visibility These are not four projects over six months. These are four steps you can start this very week! 19",
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "B2kYXI",
      "number": 20,
      "image": "decks/2026-04-22-securing-the-blind-spot-in-your-pipeline-aws-summit-london-2026/slides/020.jpg",
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "text": "Merci ! AWS CodeArtifact https://aws.amazon.com/codeartifact Datadog Code Security https://docs.datadoghq.com/security/code_security Our super interesting blog 😁 https://securitylabs.datadoghq.com 20",
      "title": ""
    }
  ],
